                    {
                        "sense_id": "25816bc7-1e64-3576-bf20-e2f96f1a7829",
                        "entry_id": "fa7051a4-b653-3128-820b-3727733b9143",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Any of a few hundred species of European and Asian plants, of the genus Verbascum, especially that majority that have yellow flowers."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdafd348-ec27-4c81-a789-4c91dd734edb",
                                "sense_id": "25816bc7-1e64-3576-bf20-e2f96f1a7829",
                                "text": "There be foure ſortes of Mulleyne, as [Pedanius] Dioſcorides writeth: wherof yͤ two firſt are white Mulleyne, and of them one is Male, and the other female: The third is blacke Mulleyne: The fourth is wilde Mulleyne. […] The white male Mulleyn (or rather Wolleyn) hath […] the whole top with his pleaſant yellow floures ſheweth like to a waxe Candell or taper cunningly wrought."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ad6d0a36-bb4d-4eca-b913-cd8af53fdbe1",
                                "sense_id": "25816bc7-1e64-3576-bf20-e2f96f1a7829",
                                "text": "As we all know, witches ride through the air on a broom, but sometimes their means of locomotion was a bulrush, a branch of thorn, mullein stalks, cornstalk, or ragweed, called fairies' horse in Ireland."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
